WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.390
From the moment she first snapped her fingers
in time to The Addams Family theme song, Christina

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.069
Ricci was a star.

00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:11.530
But despite making it to adulthood free of
scandal or addiction, it seems like Christina

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.360
Ricci just doesn't get the roles she deserves.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.730
Here's a look at why Hollywood won't cast
Christina Ricci anymore.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:20.060
Typecast

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:24.540
Christina Ricci was just nine years old when
she scored her first feature film role in

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.930
Mermaids, where she all but stole the show
from her co-stars, Winona Ryder and Cher.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:34.290
The following year, she snagged the role of
Wednesday Addams in the first Addams Family

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:39.050
movie, and her status as a pint-sized pre-teen
Hollywood icon was complete.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:42.140
But that role was actually a little too iconic.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:46.910
Even now, it's hard to shake the image of
her with that scowl and those twin black braids.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:50.850
And she hasn't been helped by the fact that
she apparently doesn't age.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:55.420
So even though it's been a quarter of a century
since Addams Family came out, fans and filmmakers

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.780
alike continue to think of her as that precocious
kid.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.680
And that kind of typecasting can be a death
sentence in Hollywood.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.689
Overcompensating

00:01:04.689 --> 00:01:09.060
In the same way certain Disney stars hit the
scandal circuit a little too hard in an effort

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:14.119
to shed their family-friendly images, Christina
Ricci went through a period in her late teens

00:01:14.119 --> 00:01:18.340
and early twenties where she really tried
to push the envelope and establish herself

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.039
as a grownup actress.

00:01:20.039 --> 00:01:25.800
The Opposite of Sex, 200 Cigarettes, Buffalo
66, and a turn in John Waters' Pecker all

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:31.390
proved that she could hang tough in dirty,
sexy, sleazy, limit-pushing roles — but

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:34.600
it also may have been a little too much at
once.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.679
Eclipsed by a Monster

00:01:36.679 --> 00:01:41.299
In 2003, Christina Ricci scored what should
have been the role that catapulted her onto

00:01:41.299 --> 00:01:46.549
the A-list: playing Selby, the girlfriend
of serial killer Aileen Wuornos, in the terrifying

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:48.020
biopic Monster.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:52.819
Only instead of earning mass accolades for
her nuanced, heartbreaking performance, Ricci

00:01:52.819 --> 00:01:57.799
went virtually unnoticed in the film — because
the performance by an almost unrecognizable

00:01:57.799 --> 00:02:00.959
Charlize Theron soaked up the entire spotlight.

00:02:00.959 --> 00:02:06.600
"My incredible, incredible leading lady, Christina
Ricci, Who I couldn't have done this film

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.600
without.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:12.000
You are truly the unsung hero of this film."

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.590
To her credit, Ricci was gracious about it,
telling The Advocate, "I like to think I also

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:20.320
made a dramatic physical transformation, so
it would hurt me a little bit when people

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:25.170
said that…but from the very beginning I
understood it was Charlize's passion project.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:29.540
I took the part of Selby knowing that I was
going to be a supporting part of that experience,

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:32.400
so it never seemed weird to me at the time."

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.420
She lost confidence

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:39.200
Many actresses struggle with body image, and
Ricci is sadly no different, telling Premiere

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.691
Magazine about her struggles with anorexia,
"I know that had I been thinner at the time

00:02:43.691 --> 00:02:48.150
my indie movies were hitting, I could've been
in a much better position in my career."

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:52.850
And she's also had issues with her height,
saying "I'm five-one first thing in the morning,

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:55.010
and I tend to look really small on camera.

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:59.420
I can probably go as far as Holly Hunter went,
then I think that's going to be it.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.860
I have a feeling I am way too small."

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.940
Well, when you're shorter than a Smurf...

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:05.940
Time off

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:11.170
After her 2012 comeback film Bel Ami flopped,
Ricci took some time off from the industry

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.480
to start a family.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:16.820
The move didn't exactly help keep her in the
Hollywood spotlight, but Ricci says it's done

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.450
wonders for her outlook on her career and
life.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:21.870
"Having a child changed everything.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:25.050
It's made everything in my life actually important
and matter.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:28.420
I now have to take things seriously, and I
never did before.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:30.030
I want to succeed for him.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.900
My choices matter more."

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.500
Second chance

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:37.480
Now that she's stopped fighting against her
public image, Ricci has begun what may be

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:42.600
a major comeback by embracing it instead,
with roles in Lizzie Borden and the TV series

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:44.660
Z: The Beginning of Everything.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.510
And her new Zen attitude shows.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:49.600
"I've always sort of trusted my instincts.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:54.220
If you do the things that you naturally gravitate
towards then there's going to be a through

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:59.310
line through your career and all your choices
are going to reflect really who you are and

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:00.380
your tastes."

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:04.650
At this point in her life — as a wife, mother,
and showbiz professional with nearly three

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:09.360
decades of experience under her belt — Ricci
knows exactly what her taste is, and what

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:12.200
kind of roles she intends to play from now
on.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.200
As she put it:

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.350
"I really love a crazy person."

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.350
Thanks for watching!

